From b52691edcdb88ed3424df6897750bc40f094b6ff Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bradent27-sketch <304192343+bradent27-sketch@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 10:17:27 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] Retire game_env (the flat game-total + venue bundle)

The bundled "market total + roof/venue" multiplier (_game_env_multiplier: implied-total elasticity per position x an indoor/outdoor
factor, VENUE_MULT QB 1.049/0.981, TE 1.037/0.986, WR 1.028/0.989, RB neutral) was built, measured and rejected as a bundle (+0.012 MAE).
Its halves were then tested alone: v2_game_total_elasticity was superseded by the shipped per-stat version, v2_venue_mult was
INCONCLUSIVE (retired in the first wave). Nothing in the default model used the flat multiplier, so the flat environment multiplier was
already 1.0 everywhere; the per-stat implied-total channel is unchanged. Removes _game_env_multiplier, VENUE_MULT, the use_total /
use_venue plumbing, one test, and the wave-1 flag names left behind in the env-loading condition. The 'environment_status' text stays
'feature disabled' (the UI shows it). GAME_TOTAL_ELASTICITY / GAME_TOTAL_CLIP stay: the per-stat table falls back to them.
Restore with git revert of this commit.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
